## 6. Host app (ApexBroker)

Tabs: **Dashboard, Portfolio, SIPs, Goals, Activity.** Header: logo, tabs, working bell (list of check-in reminders), user menu.

- **Dashboard:** greeting, summary cards (total portfolio, available cash, monthly SIPs), allocation donut (legend colours must match segments), active SIP list, goal progress.
- **Portfolio:** summary cards + holdings table with **Buy More** and **Withdraw** per row.
- **SIPs:** one card per SIP (fund, amount, status, next debit, linked goal, total invested) with **Pause SIP** and **Reduce SIP** (Resume button when paused).
- **Goals:** goal cards with progress %, target, date, monthly contribution, status chip (On track / Slightly behind / At risk).
- **Activity:** transaction log + **Decision Records** (the user's Decision Memory, with delete) + 30-day check-ins.

**Triggers:** `Pause SIP`, `Reduce SIP` and `Withdraw` open **FinPilot**. **Add Investment** (Dashboard button), **Buy More** and **Start new SIP** open a plain host dialog (no FinPilot modal).

**Add Investment dialog:** pick fund, type any amount (plus quick chips ₹5,000 / ₹10,000 / ₹25,000), One-time or Monthly SIP, Confirm. Under the amount show **one live, non-blocking line** tagged "FinPilot insight", using the same engine:
- Monthly SIP: *"This adds ₹X/month to {goal} and brings your goal about N months earlier."*
- One-time: *"This adds ₹X toward {goal}, about N months closer."*
Empty/invalid amount → *"Enter an amount to see the impact."* It never blocks Confirm. One-time updates holding, cash, total; Monthly creates/updates a SIP. Both log to Activity.

**After any FinPilot decision the host updates everything** from shared state: SIP status/amount (paused badge reads **"Paused until {date} · auto-resumes"**), holdings, cash, goal corpus/contribution/progress/status, dashboard totals, Activity log, and a **30-day check-in** ("Ready to resume your SIP?" / "Review your withdrawal"). Show a toast: *"Saved to your decision records."*

